Bug 2029781 - Respect the 55-character limit when hashing names with illegal characters. r=tobyp

NS_MsgHashIfNecessary truncates a folder name that contains an illegal
character (such as ':') at that character before appending the 8 hex
digits of the hash. For a name whose illegal character is at or beyond
the 47-character cap this produced an on-disk name longer than MAX_LEN
(55) characters, e.g. a 125-character name kept 117 characters plus the
hash. That is how a folder like 'Effectiveness of an automated
intervention ... settings: a multicentre randomised controlled trial'
ended up stored under a 125-character name that itself contained the
old hash.

Cap the kept length at MAX_LEN - 8 like the plain too-long branch; the
hash is still computed over the full original name, so the resulting
on-disk name is the same as for any other 55+ character name. Drop one
character further when it would otherwise end in the high surrogate of
a surrogate pair, as the too-long branch already does.

Add a gtest for the new behaviour and an xpcshell test asserting that
a folder whose illegal character lies past the cap is stored under a
55-character name.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318580

diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgUtils.cpp b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgUtils.cpp
--- a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgUtils.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgUtils.cpp
@@ -296,12 +296,16 @@ nsString NS_MsgHashIfNecessary(const nsA
   }
 
   char hashedname[9];
   int32_t keptLength = -1;
-  if (illegalCharacterIndex != -1)
-    keptLength = illegalCharacterIndex;
-  else if (name.Length() > MAX_LEN) {
+  if (illegalCharacterIndex != -1) {
+    // The name is truncated at the illegal character, but never beyond the
+    // length limit: the hashed name must fit within MAX_LEN like any other.
+    keptLength = std::min(illegalCharacterIndex, (int32_t)MAX_LEN - 8);
+  } else if (name.Length() > MAX_LEN) {
     keptLength = MAX_LEN - 8;
+  }
+  if (keptLength == (int32_t)MAX_LEN - 8) {
     // To avoid keeping only the high surrogate of a surrogate pair
     if (NS_IS_HIGH_SURROGATE(name.CharAt(keptLength - 1))) --keptLength;
   }
 
